{"id":"chatcmpl-7a1ead72-d4b9-4811-b88a-1478f960f230","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229337,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When a visual finding's laterality is ambiguous on a lateral view, the successful strategy was to triangulate multiple independent visual-language assessments and targeted region-of-interest inspection rather than trusting a single model output. The workflow combined expert-model queries, independent VLM cross-checks, and zoomed pixel inspection to resolve left/right ambiguity before committing to an answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a single model gives a confident but ambiguity-prone answer (e.g., laterality on a lateral view), query multiple independent visual models and require convergent evidence before finalizing.\",\n    \"When spatial laterality is uncertain, use region-of-interest cropping/zooming to directly inspect the relevant anatomy rather than relying on whole-image model judgments.\",\n    \"Frame follow-up queries around anatomical landmarks (spine, diaphragm, anterior/posterior position) to convert vague opacity descriptions into localizable evidence.\",\n    \"Treat a proposed answer as a hypothesis to audit: explicitly flag the risk (e.g., left/right confusion) and design verification steps that could falsify it.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Triangulate across multiple independent vision-language models; use ROI zoom on ambiguous regions; anchor descriptions to anatomical landmarks.\",\n    \"Ambiguous spatial reasoning tasks\": \"Identify the specific ambiguity (laterality, depth, orientation), then gather independent evidence sources and inspect the region directly before answering.\",\n    \"Multi-tool verification workflows\": \"Use one tool to propose, others to independently verify, and a zoom/crop step to ground the decision in pixel evidence; require convergence before finalizing.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the proposed finding is supported by at least two independent assessments and direct ROI inspection.\",\n    \"Explicitly check for the known ambiguity risk (e.g., left vs right on lateral view) using anatomical landmarks before committing.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1005,"total_tokens":1398,"completion_tokens":393,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":1005},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":393}}}